@* Upstream's "Menu" is a menu bar rather than a menu: three labelled columns divided by vertical
   rules, which is where a vertical separator actually earns its place. This used to draw a fake
   dropdown with a horizontal rule in it — a different component wearing this one's name.

   The last rule and the last column are hidden below md, so the row narrows to two by dropping a
   pair rather than by wrapping. *@
<div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm md:gap-4">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
        <span class="font-medium">Settings</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Manage preferences</span>
    </div>
    <Separator Orientation="vertical" />
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
        <span class="font-medium">Account</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Profile &amp; security</span>
    </div>
    <Separator Orientation="vertical" Class="hidden md:block" />
    <div class="hidden flex-col gap-1 md:flex">
        <span class="font-medium">Help</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Support &amp; docs</span>
    </div>
</div>
